  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "dmhc-action-mix",
      "text": "DMHC Office of Enforcement published 5,435 enforcement-action rows from 2000-07-03 through 2026-05-22. Source-native classes include Letter of Agreement 4,212, Settlement Agreement 606, Cease and Desist Order 240, and Accusation 53, plus every other official class in the file. Those 5,435 rows name 238 distinct organization-name strings. A letter of agreement is not a settlement. An accusation is not a final finding. A cease-and-desist order is not a revocation. An enforcement occurrence is not a unique company. This is not an insurer ranking."
    },
    {
      "id": "imr-volume",
      "text": "DMHC Independent Medical Review determinations total 42,749 rows (datastore as of 2026-06-01). Overturned decision of health plan: 22,445. Upheld decision of health plan: 20,304. An IMR case is not a complaint. An IMR decision is not enforcement. An IMR outcome is not a plan quality score. IMR volume is not market share. This extract has no plan identifier and no enrollment denominator, so plan-level IMR rates are not published."
    },
    {
      "id": "cdi-health-list",
      "text": "CDI's dated health-insurer list names 28 companies licensed to provide health insurance coverage as of 2025-12-31. 28 have a published business phone and 27 have a website. Licensed is not currently selling. This list is not the complete admitted-carrier universe and is not the DMHC Knox-Keene plan roster."
    },
    {
      "id": "fair-plan-residual",
      "text": "CDI's January 2025 fact sheet on residential policies reports 324,954 FAIR Plan new-and-renewed policies in 2023 versus 8,300,730 in the voluntary market (3.7% of that residential new-and-renewed mix). FAIR Plan is residual-market infrastructure, not the typical California insurance market, not an insurer of choice, and not a safety score."
    }
  ],
